    "methods_description": "EEG data were recorded from 56 healthy participants (60 sessions total) using a 64-channel EEG system during speech perception and silent speech production tasks. The experimental protocol consisted of four segments: rest (5 s with fixation cross), perception (4-5 s with 6-7 sentence repetitions), preparation (1 s blank screen), and silent speech production (5 s). Participants listened to spoken Spanish sentences and then silently repeated them without motor action. Trials were presented in randomized order across 30 stimuli per block.",
